From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SushyDev <mail@sushy.dev>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 23:09:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: prefer a lower bit depth over compression

msm_dp_panel_dsc_possible() asks whether the mode fits at the bit depth
the EDID advertises.  A monitor advertising 10 bpc makes 3440x1440@120
look like 698750 * 30 = 20.96 Gbps against a 16.87 Gbps budget, so DSC
is engaged, even though the same mode fits uncompressed at 8 bpc:
698750 * 24 = 16.77 Gbps.

msm_dp_panel_get_mode_bpp() already steps bpp down until a mode fits, it
just never got the chance because the DSC test ran first.  Ask whether
the mode fits at the minimum RGB depth instead, so compression is
reserved for modes that cannot be sent uncompressed at all.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c
index 455b9b4..38ca802 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c
@@ -285,7 +285,7 @@ bool msm_dp_panel_dsc_possible(struct msm_dp_panel *msm_dp_panel,
 
 	return source_bpp >= 24 &&
 		(u64)mode_pclk_khz * 8 <= link_rate &&
-		(u64)mode_pclk_khz * source_bpp > link_rate;
+		(u64)mode_pclk_khz * 24u > link_rate;
 }
 
 static const struct {
